# docs/matrix-engine/tools/label_census.allow
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Allow-list for label_census.sh / label_census.py: citation sites where the
# TOKEN "label" looks like a real label (it survives normalisation as a valid
# identifier: /^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_:]*$/) but is not one.
#
# VERIFIED: docs/latex/gl2_contract.tex defines no `\label{label}` (429 labels
# total at the WP-10 close). Every site below is prose EXPLAINING the
# `[C, label]` citation syntax itself, using the literal word "label" as the
# generic placeholder -- not a citation of an actual contract statement. (Every
# OTHER placeholder spelling found in the tree -- `[C, <label>]`, `[C, \ldots]`,
# `[C, …]`, the macro body `[C,~\texttt{#1}]`, `\HA{$\cdot$}` -- already fails
# the identifier check on its own, via the `<`/`>`/backslash/ellipsis/`$`
# characters, and needs no allow-list entry; see label_census.py's module
# docstring for the tokeniser.)
#
# FORMAT (content-keyed, hecke-extensions slot 4 WP-6): one
# `relpath|<verbatim fragment of the site's source line>` entry per line
# (relpath relative to the repository root), preceded by a `#` reason. An
# entry matches every UNRESOLVED citation whose full source line contains the
# fragment -- so it survives lines being inserted or deleted above the cited
# passage, unlike the retired `relpath:line` form (WP-10's original format,
# which this migration replaces; label_census.py now REJECTS a `relpath:line`
# entry with a named error rather than silently reinterpreting or skipping
# it). An entry that matches zero sites is STALE and fails the census.
#
# THE UNIT OF PROGRESS is removing an entry -- e.g. if a document's prose is
# rewritten to use `<label>` or `\ldots` instead of the bare word "label",
# its allow-list line is deleted along with the fix (and would otherwise be
# reported STALE, since it would then match nothing).
#
# A planted BAD citation (a real-looking but undefined label, e.g.
# `[C, no_such_label]`) is NOT covered by any entry here and must still fail
# label_census.sh -- that is ContractCensusValidation's negative-control arm.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

